#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059615 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b082a95-4d6e-512f-a6ed-9100498d17c8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions"}] :question/id #uuid "6e647031-a93a-54b7-8b39-c6d3779a48ab" :question/math-academy-id "e-7008" :question/problem "If $X = \\{ a, b, c, d, e, f, g \\},$ which of the following collections of subsets of $X$ are partitions of $X?$\n\nI. $\\{ a, b, \\{ c,d,e \\}, \\{ f,g \\} \\}$\n\nII. $\\{ \\{ a, b, c \\}, \\{ d,e,f \\}, \\{ g \\} \\}$\n\nIII. $\\{ \\emptyset, \\{ a,b,c \\}, \\{ f,g \\} \\}$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each collection of subsets.\n\n- Collection I is *not* a partition because $a$ and $b$ are not subsets.\n\n- Collection II is a partition. All the subsets are non-empty, and every element of $X$ is contained in exactly one subset.\n\n- Collection III is *not* a partition. The subset $\\emptyset$ is empty, and the elements $d$ and $e$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059616 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c1d9899-21e8-5ab1-9bc5-10e4a8100ed9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Set to Form a Partition"}] :question/id #uuid "fcf768ea-80dc-5238-9694-883204f8f1f8" :question/math-academy-id "e-7009" :question/problem "Consider the set $X = \\{ -4, -1, 2, 5, 8, 11, 14, 17 \\}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n\\{ \\{ -1, 5, 8 \\}, \\{ -4, 11 \\}, \\{ 14 \\}, \\, \\_\\_\\_\\_ \\, \\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nIn order to find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $-4 \\in \\{ -4, 11 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $-1 \\in \\{ -1, 5, 8 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $2$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\n- $5 \\in \\{ -1, 5, 8 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $8 \\in \\{ -1, 5, 8 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $11 \\in \\{ -4, 11 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $14 \\in \\{ 14 \\} \\quad \\color{green}\\checkmark$\n\n- $17$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\quad \\color{red}\\times$\n\nThe elements $2$ and $17$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{ 2,17 \\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059617 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b2a9a1d-2d20-58cf-a1ee-bee2f4cf120d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of Large Sets"}] :question/id #uuid "e0696e3c-de10-5b18-ba67-1d381ddbe0be" :question/math-academy-id "e-7010" :question/problem "If $X = \\{ 5, 10, 15, \\ldots, 50 \\},$ which of the following collections of subsets of $X$ are partitions of $X?$\n\nI. $\\{ \\{ 5, 10 \\}, \\{ 15, 20, 25, \\ldots, 45 \\}, \\{ 50 \\} \\}$\n\nII. $\\{ \\{ 5, 10, 15, \\ldots, 30 \\}, \\{ 40, 45, 50 \\} \\}$\n\nIII. $\\{ \\{ 5, 10, 15, \\ldots, 50 \\} \\}$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect each collection of subsets.\n\n- Collection I is a partition. All the subsets are non-empty, and every element of $X$ is contained in exactly one subset.\n\n- Collection II is *not* a partition because the element $35$ does not appear in any subsets.\n\n- Collection III is a partition. There is only one subset, but that is okay. The subset is non-empty, and every element of $X$ is contained in this subset.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371506 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c1d9899-21e8-5ab1-9bc5-10e4a8100ed9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Set to Form a Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c1615d1-6030-599d-aeec-a3e098b0f772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{6,9,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496680} {:answer/id #uuid "59008d48-df74-5294-8d7b-477225578643" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{3,6,9\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496847} {:answer/id #uuid "b34bdc7c-ae2a-5c5a-a2f1-547394871f6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{5,6,9,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497024} {:answer/id #uuid "ecba50d7-df68-57d6-827a-9babc3cd9a74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{6,9\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497165} {:answer/id #uuid "ee3c953b-6c20-50a4-8eb5-a2a98b6cfbbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{9,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497169}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c1615d1-6030-599d-aeec-a3e098b0f772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{6,9,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496680} :answer-field/id #uuid "63bac6c5-dd87-541d-a9ea-3996685c77b1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371507}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bc1a812c-1051-5f8d-9b27-1018f3b5ca90" :question/math-academy-id "q-105868" :question/problem "Consider the set $X=\\{0,1,2,3,…,10\\}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\{2,3,5,7\\},\\{0,1\\},\\,\\{4,8\\},\\,____\\,\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $0\\in \\{0,1\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\in \\{0,1\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $2\\in \\{2,3,5,7\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $3\\in \\{2,3,5,7\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $4\\in \\{4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $5\\in \\{2,3,5,7\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $6$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $7\\in \\{2,3,5,7\\}$\n\n- $8\\in \\{4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $9$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\n- $10$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe elements $6,9,$ and $10$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{6,9,10\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386161 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8c1d9899-21e8-5ab1-9bc5-10e4a8100ed9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Missing Set to Form a Partition"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40b86896-0300-577a-979e-abac89657737" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{2,6,10\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496798} {:answer/id #uuid "5bcfc04b-0b2a-555c-a63a-74a796d45448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{14\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496859} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb15e11-3c07-541f-b460-d1774b41a3e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{10,14\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496899} {:answer/id #uuid "ce6be59f-a904-501e-934c-2735386e9572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{6,14\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497083} {:answer/id #uuid "d97fa492-a629-547f-8684-c44665ed797e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{6,10,14\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497117}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bcfc04b-0b2a-555c-a63a-74a796d45448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{14\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496859} :answer-field/id #uuid "9763950a-9d31-5794-bcc0-4622ea09bfb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386162}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29332e57-5723-57e4-a031-105647b85293" :question/math-academy-id "q-105877" :question/problem "Consider the set $X=\\{2,4,6,8,10,12,14\\}.$ Which subset must be placed into the blank in the set below so that it represents a partition of $X?$\n\n$$\n\\{\\{2,4,8\\},\\{6,12\\},\\,\\{10\\},\\,____\\,\\}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $X$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $X$ where every element of $X$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nTo find the subset that goes in the blank, we must identify which elements of $X$ are not yet contained within any of the given subsets.\n\nLet's go through each element of $X$ and check:\n\n- $2\\in \\{2,4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $4\\in \\{2,4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $6\\in \\{6,12\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $8\\in \\{2,4,8\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $10\\in \\{10\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $12\\in \\{6,12\\}\\,✓$\n\n- $14$ does not belong to any of the given subsets $\\,\\times $\n\nThe element $14$ is not yet contained within any of the given subsets. Therefore, the subset that must go in the blank is $\\{14\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417775 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1b082a95-4d6e-512f-a6ed-9100498d17c8" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "704abcbb-66b9-523f-8075-50f9a4a8256e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{0,10\\},\\{2,4,6,8\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496901} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1a3d01-2cd6-5dd9-89b9-88a328e0be94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{0,10\\},\\{2,4,6,8,10\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497012} {:answer/id #uuid "dcb8ade0-cb28-5bda-9bc7-ef18d90e2205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{0,2,4,6,8,10,12\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497128} {:answer/id #uuid "ee2438de-047c-5102-97a9-b54926d28ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{∅,\\{0,2,4,6,8\\},\\{10\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497168} {:answer/id #uuid "f914fa50-6ac0-566e-b1a1-d5f660016346" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{0,10\\},\\{2\\},\\{4,8,10\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497192}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "704abcbb-66b9-523f-8075-50f9a4a8256e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{0,10\\},\\{2,4,6,8\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496901} :answer-field/id #uuid "50e0add4-d87e-54cf-8530-185be76bcd24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "84e33efb-d3f8-5005-acd9-dce160c0ccce" :question/math-academy-id "q-105882" :question/problem "If $T=\\{0,2,4,6,8,10\\}$, which collection of subsets of $T$ is a partition of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "A partition of a set $T$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $T$ where every element of $T$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only $\\{\\{0,10\\},\\{2,4,6,8\\}\\}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- $\\{∅,\\{0,2,4,6,8\\},\\{10\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the subset $∅$ is empty.\n\n- $\\{\\{0,2,4,6,8,10,12\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the element $12$ does not appear in $T.$\n\n- $\\{\\{0,10\\},\\{2\\},\\{4,8\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the element $6\\in T$ does not appear in any subset.\n\n- $\\{\\{0,10\\},\\{2,4,6,8,10\\}\\}$ is not a partition because the element $10$ appears in two subsets."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371520 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b2a9a1d-2d20-58cf-a1ee-bee2f4cf120d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Partitions of Large Sets"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2341484c-7c9c-5124-be30-56d366c22197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{2,4,6,…,100\\},\\{5,15,25…,95\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496732} {:answer/id #uuid "90228f19-45d5-5153-a3be-5c943b8968b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{2,4,6,…,40\\},\\{1,2,3,…,99\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186496958} {:answer/id #uuid "d78b5b70-e4dd-50f6-8a29-71cf38eb844d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{0,1,2,3,…,100\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497111} {:answer/id #uuid "f1170470-f90c-5756-b084-7fa97b0e9c40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\{\\{2,4,6,…,100\\},\\{1,3,5,…,99\\}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186497177} {:answer/id #uuid "fa465f11-09e6-50fc-840b-b4b8607f